### Form Integration

Set `name` on `NumberField.Root` and leave the surrounding `Field.Root` unnamed. This submits one
canonical numeric value while preserving the visible input's form owner and Enter submission.
A named `Field.Root` currently gives both the visible input and the hidden numeric input the same
name, producing duplicate form entries; formatted input can also submit locale-specific text.

```svelte
<Field.Root>
  <NumberField.Root name="quantity" defaultValue={1} min={1} max={100}>
    <NumberField.ScrubArea label="Quantity" />
    <NumberField.Group>
      <NumberField.Decrement />
      <NumberField.Input />
      <NumberField.Increment />
    </NumberField.Group>
  </NumberField.Root>
</Field.Root>
```

An unnamed field does not associate server errors by field name. If your form uses server errors,
handle their display and invalid state explicitly. The example below validates the submitted
quantity and shows a success alert; it does not render `Field.Error`.

